      "sourceTextSha256": "7dd70bd3237b6920993a4e6a51b0586f0975c9f9b0a3d3e37e79883a9ccd56f6",
      "text": "Day 3 · After breakfast, full-day excursion to Valparaíso and Viña del Mar, through the olive groves, orchards and vineyards of the Curacaví and Casablanca valleys (120 km from Santiago). Built on 42 hills, Valparaíso is a UNESCO World Heritage Site, its levels linked by historic lifts, funiculars, stairways and paths. Visit Plaza Sotomayor and its national-monument Maritime Authority building, walk up Cerro Concepción along the Gervasoni and Atkinson promenades for a magnificent view of the port, and visit La Sebastiana, Pablo Neruda’s house. Continue to Viña del Mar, the “Garden City”, with its beaches and cliffs, the flower clock, Reñaca Beach, the promenade and the Fonck Museum. Return to Santiago.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1aWUbUU6YPlsMBoyRKpXYQxnELzXegGOR",
        "documentSha256": "cd5c9d0e54f0166e1c3ed8f6c03be635dc44daca3563550e3450f0cca8520dae",
